      "text": "El Calafate and the Perito Moreno Glacier",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "word_aligned",
        "fileId": "1SPGT__blzqTlUv3YSanLfbodva2V_yP1",
        "documentSha256": "62fcfbb0d7f13629ff21d0de097b1227ecf846e24881389aa85a2197394ffab6",
        "paragraphs": [
          {
            "ref": "text:Day 10 · Breakfast. Full-day excursion to the walkways of the Perito Moreno Glacier, including the “Safari Náutico” boat trip. Drive 80 km to Los Glaciares National Park, a UNESCO World Heritage Site preserving a vast area of the continental ice field, from which the Moreno, Onelli, Agassiz and Upsala glaciers descend. The Perito Moreno spreads over Lago Argentino with a wall about 5 km wide and up to 70 metres high, in shades from pure white to turquoise.",
            "textSha256": "501a104fe3368789be2877eb20550f8812e092b2e4e762bee5f3022e37774167"
          }
        ],
